          "source": "",
          "thread": "fee switch governance failures",
          "why": "Two separate fee switch proposals failing drew combined 736 clicks — readers are tracking whether UNI holders can ever actually capture protocol revenue."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "regulatory pressure Wells Notice CFTC",
          "why": "The SEC Wells Notice and CFTC fine landed in the same window, making Uniswap the highest-profile DeFi enforcement target, which readers followed closely for precedent."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Labs unilateral UI fee extraction",
          "why": "Uniswap Labs charging a 0.25% UI fee without a DAO vote — then hitting $1M in a month — crystallized the Labs-vs-protocol tension readers were already tracking."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "V4 launch and Unichain expansion",
          "why": "Hooks architecture, a new L2, and a $165M treasury plan gave readers a concrete product narrative to follow across multiple months of previews and launches."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "mainstream brokerage integration",
          "why": "The Robinhood partnership was the single most-clicked Uniswap headline, signaling readers see retail distribution as the breakout story above all protocol internals."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "DAO power concentration and exits",
          "why": "Governance rights being relegated toward Optimism stakeholders and a prominent contributor publicly quitting revealed structural capture that readers found more alarming than routine governance votes."
        }
      ]
    },
